# Knowledge pack J (21 Nov 2026): Gog and Magog (Ya'juj and Ma'juj).
# Sourced from assets/stories/layers/gog-magog.json (checked 2026-10-20).
# The digging narration (tirmidhi 3153, ibnmajah 4080) is left out: graders differ.

E('gog-and-magog',
  m=[r'\b(?:gog and magog|gog magog|gog n magog|yajuj|yajooj|ya juj|majuj|majooj|ma juj|magog)\b',
     r'\bdhul ?qarnayn\b.*\b(?:wall|barrier|dam)\b', r'\b(?:wall|barrier|dam)\b.*\bdhul ?qarnayn\b',
     r'\bwall of (?:gog|dhul ?qarnayn)\b'],
  x=[r'\bsons? of (?:nuh|noah)\b', r'\b(?:nuh|noah)s? sons?\b', r'\bdescend\w*\b'],
  topic='Gog and Magog',
  go=['/stories', '/quran', '/hadith'],
  text="""
Gog and Magog (Ya'juj and Ma'juj) are two peoples in the Qur'an. A people who met Dhul-Qarnayn asked him for protection from their corruption, so he built a barrier between two mountains ({QR 18:93-97}). Ibn Kathir says they are among the children of Adam, and describes the barrier as iron blocks piled up with molten copper poured over them.

He told them it was a mercy from his Lord, and that when the promise of his Lord comes, He will level it ({QR 18:98}). That is one of the signs of the Last Hour: they will be released and rush down from every height ({QR 21:96-97}).

The Prophet ﷺ came alarmed and said that a gap the size of a circle made with his fingers had opened in the barrier of Gog and Magog. Zaynab bint Jahsh asked whether they would be destroyed while the righteous were among them, and he said yes, when wickedness increases ({HS bukhari:3598|Zaynab bint Jahsh reported that the Prophet came alarmed and said a gap the size of the circle he made with his fingers had opened in the barrier of Gog and Magog; destruction comes when wickedness increases}). Muslim records the same report ({HS muslim:2880|the same report of the gap in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj}). Their release and destruction after the Dajjal and the descent of Isa is in the long report of al-Nawwas ibn Sam'an ({HS muslim:2937|the long report on the Dajjal, the descent of Isa, and the release and destruction of Gog and Magog before the Last Hour}).

Which son of Nuh are they from? Ma'ariful Qur'an says most hadith scholars and historians trace them to Yafith (Japheth), son of Nuh. That is the scholars' view; the Qur'an does not name their line.

Where is the barrier? Scholars differ. Ma'ariful Qur'an mentions walls near Darband in Daghestan or in the Caucasus, and rejects the Great Wall of China. The text itself gives no definite place, and whether they have already emerged is also discussed, so I will not name a place or a date.

For the whole story, with the places and the different views, open Stories.
""",
  review='Scholar review needed: the location and whether they have already emerged are disputed; answer states only what the sources state.')
